## Overview

In this case, it displays the most recent logs from the past 30 days.
Generated by sshd
Errors containing 'Failed password'

    | extend AttackerIP = extract(@“from\s+((?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3})”, 1, SyslogMessage) This part is key:
    When a log entry of this type occurs:

        Failed password for invalid user admin from 192.168.1.50 port 54321 ssh2
    Extract only the generated IP address (192.168.1.50)

Sample the following fields:
    TimeGenerated,
    Computer,
    SyslogMessage
Finally, sort them from newest to oldest.

All of this forms the basis of our detection for failed SSH login attempts.

```kusto
Syslog
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where ProcessName == "sshd"
| where SyslogMessage has "Failed password"
| extend AttackerIP = extract(@"from\s+((?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3})", 1, SyslogMessage)
| where isnotempty(AttackerIP)
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    Computer,
    AttackerIP,
    SyslogMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc
```